  "conflicts": [
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_312",
      "clause_b": "bgb_327",
      "description": "The cross-reference in bgb_327(3) to bgb_312(1a) creates a dependency loop where the scope of digital products is defined by the scope of general consumer contracts, which in turn are often interpreted in light of the specific provisions for digital products."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_356",
      "clause_b": "bgb_312f",
      "description": "The mechanism for the expiration of the right of withdrawal for digital content is tightly coupled to the confirmation duty in §312f. If the confirmation is not provided, the right of withdrawal does not expire, creating a potential 'infinite' withdrawal window if the entrepreneur fails to comply with the §312f procedural requirements."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_312g",
      "clause_b": "bgb_495",
      "description": "The interaction between the general withdrawal right in § 312g and the specific loan-based withdrawal right in § 495 requires careful navigation of § 312g(3) to avoid overlapping or conflicting information duties."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_327",
      "clause_b": "bgb_312",
      "description": "Potential for regulatory collision regarding 'digital products' vs 'services' where both statutes claim application, specifically regarding data-for-service contracts."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_327(5)",
      "clause_b": "bgb_327c",
      "description": "§327(5) creates a specific exclusion for physical data carriers regarding the rights in §327c, which is a critical boundary condition for contract termination rights."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_327",
      "clause_b": "bgb_327c",
      "description": "§327(5) explicitly excludes §327c from applying to physical data carriers, creating a potential gap for consumers if a physical carrier is never delivered."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_327n",
      "clause_b": "bgb_327m",
      "description": "Potential for circularity in logic: bgb_327n (1) references bgb_327m (2) to override exclusion rules, while bgb_327m (3) references bgb_327o for post-termination recovery. If the definitions of 'termination' or 'defect' are updated in 327m, 327n's reduction logic may become structurally unstable."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_358",
      "clause_b": "bgb_356",
      "description": "The cross-reference in bgb_358(4) to bgb_356(5) creates a complex valuation dependency for digital content in connected contracts, which may lead to ambiguity if the underlying digital content contract is terminated under different provisions."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_491",
      "clause_b": "bgb_358",
      "description": "bgb_491(4) removes the protection of bgb_358 for court-settled loans, potentially leaving the consumer without a remedy for the connected contract."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_358",
      "clause_b": "bgb_506",
      "description": "bgb_358(3) defines 'economic unit' primarily through the lens of loan-based financing. bgb_506 applies this to other financing aids without explicit adjustment for non-loan structures, creating ambiguity in the definition of 'economic unit' for non-loan financing."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_491",
      "clause_b": "bgb_495",
      "description": "The interaction between the definition of 'Immobiliar-Verbraucherdarlehensverträge' in bgb_491 and the withdrawal exceptions in bgb_495 creates ambiguity regarding the applicability of the 7-day cooling-off period for specific sub-types of loans."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_491a",
      "clause_b": "bgb_495",
      "description": "The requirement to provide a contract draft in bgb_491a(2) is conditional on the existence of a withdrawal right under bgb_495, yet bgb_495(2) uses compliance with bgb_491a as a condition to exclude that very withdrawal right."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_504",
      "clause_b": "bgb_495",
      "description": "Cross-referencing exclusions between § 504 Abs. 2 and § 495 Abs. 2 create a complex conditional loop that complicates the determination of the right of withdrawal for specific short-term credit products."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_491",
      "clause_b": "bgb_358",
      "description": "The threshold exclusions in bgb_491(2) create a structural gap where a contract might be economically linked (bgb_358) but legally excluded from the withdrawal protections intended for consumer loans."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_505",
      "clause_b": "bgb_495",
      "description": "The curing provision in bgb_505 (textual addition) conflicts with the strict exclusion of withdrawal rights in bgb_495(2)(3), as it is unclear if the curing period suspends the exclusion or if the exclusion remains absolute regardless of the cure."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_495",
      "clause_b": "bgb_504",
      "description": "Circular reference and potential conflict: §495(2) No. 3 excludes the withdrawal right for contracts corresponding to §504(2), while §504(2) explicitly excludes the application of §495. This creates a recursive definition problem."
    },
    {
      "clause_a": "bgb_358",
      "clause_b": "bgb_360",
      "description": "The distinction between 'verbundene Verträge' (§ 358) and 'zusammenhängende Verträge' (§ 360) is highly fact-dependent. In the context of § 506 financing, the boundary between these two is prone to litigation as it determines whether the stricter § 358 rules or the broader § 360 rules apply."
    },
    {
